    <ns3:Definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An Adverse Outcome Pathway (AOP) is a conceptual framework that portrays existing knowledge concerning the linkage between two anchor points - the Molecular Initiating Event (MIE), and an Adverse Outcome (AO), connected by a chain of Key Events (KE) and the relationships between them (KER).</ns3:Definition>
